<CourseLayout title="Recover the impossible." description="Operation Last Light. Four roles, six areas and the last intact research archive at Meridian Station." eyebrow="THE FINAL MISSION / MERIDIAN" wide>
<section class="callout"><h2>This is your final mission: Operation Last Light.</h2><p>Recover Meridian Station's archive using the skills from all twelve weeks. The demonstration below, <strong>Operation Lamplight</strong>, is a different worked example. Your playable Last Light trial begins beneath it.</p><ol><li><strong>Start or resume.</strong> For a first rehearsal, choose Baseline, select Start new trial and confirm if prompted. Then choose the Declared recovery objective before selecting a role or operating equipment. Saved work resumes automatically with its initial objective locked; start a new trial to choose a different objective.</li><li><strong>Preserve the plan and a revision.</strong> Before practical checks, the Coordinator records Version 1 at Dispatch. Return later to record an explained revision, keeping the original.</li><li><strong>Follow the Mission Journal.</strong> Read the new manifest and map. Verify the signed archive profile before using it to configure the cradle, test a route and hand over. Go to each objective for its role and controls. Solo practice lets you switch roles; teams share one browser and rotate control.</li><li><strong>Finish and keep the record.</strong> Complete the common objectives, then record the evidence for physical custody, digital receipt or stable handover at Dispatch. Resolve that outcome, read the debrief and export. Write the team explanation after playing.</li></ol><p><a href={withBase("/assessments/final-project/")}>Read the full final-project steps and submission checklist →</a></p></section>
<DemonstrationLink id="assessment-final"/>
<Mission kind="recovery"/>
</CourseLayout>
